Mitsuba 3 is a research-oriented rendering system for forward and
inverse light transport simulation. It consists of a small set of core
libraries and a wide variety of plugins that implement functionality
ranging from materials and light sources to complete rendering
algorithms. It is retargetable: the same code can be compiled into
scalar (one ray at a time), vectorized JIT (LLVM on the CPU, Metal on
Apple GPUs) and differentiable variants, built on the Dr.Jit compiler.

This package provides the Python module and the mitsuba command-line
renderer with the scalar_rgb, scalar_spectral, llvm_ad_rgb and
llvm_ad_spectral variants, plus metal_ad_rgb on macOS.
